{"title":"Longest Subsequence That Is a Substring","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given two strings `X` and `Y`. Find the length of the **longest subsequence of `X` that is also a substring of `Y`**.\n\nIn other words, find the largest `L` such that some block of `L` consecutive characters of `Y` can be obtained from `X` by deleting characters (possibly none) without reordering the rest. The characters of that block do not have to be adjacent in `X`, but they must appear in `X` in the same order as in `Y`.\n\nPrint `L`. If no character of `Y` occurs in `X`, print `0`.","inputFormat":"Line 1: the string `X`.\nLine 2: the string `Y`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the length of the longest subsequence of `X` that is a substring of `Y`.","constraints":["1 ≤ |X|, |Y| ≤ 1000","`X` and `Y` consist of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"abcde\nxbdz","output":"2","explanation":"`bd` is a substring of `xbdz`, and it is a subsequence of `abcde` (b at position 2, d at position 4). Any longer block of `xbdz` contains `x` or `z`, which are not in `abcde`."},{"input":"abab\nbaba","output":"3","explanation":"`aba` is a substring of `baba` and a subsequence of `abab` (indices 0, 1, 2). The whole of `baba` fails: after matching `b`, `a`, `b` in `abab` there is no `a` left."},{"input":"xyz\nabc","output":"0","explanation":"`Y` shares no characters with `X`."}],"tests":[{"input":"a\na","output":"1"},{"input":"a\nb","output":"0"},{"input":"aaaa\naa","output":"2"},{"input":"ab\nabab","output":"2"},{"input":"cbdadabacbab\nabbbaab","output":"5"},{"input":"bbbbababaaaa\nabbabaaa","output":"7"},{"input":"ac\nbc","output":"1"},{"input":"b\nbaabbaabb","output":"1"},{"input":"bbbaaaac\naccc","output":"2"},{"input":"baaaabbababbbb\nbabbbababbb","output":"9"},{"input":"abbbaabaabb\nbbabbabb","output":"6"},{"input":"bababbccbacda\ncab","output":"2"},{"input":"cbabcbcbaaccbb\naabbbbcbabbc","output":"8"},{"input":"baaaaaa\na","output":"1"},{"input":"bbaababaaa\nabaaaba","output":"6"},{"input":"addad\nbaacbcaccd","output":"2"},{"input":"accb\nac","output":"2"},{"input":"baaacabcbac\nbcbcb","output":"5"},{"input":"\","output":"541"},{"input":"\","output":"54"},{"input":"\","output":"1000"},{"input":"\","output":"999"}],"complexity":{"time":"O(|X| · |Y|)","space":"O(|Y|)"},"hints":["A substring of `Y` is fixed by where it ends. Let `dp[i][j]` be the longest suffix of `Y[0..j)` that is a subsequence of `X[0..i)`.","If `X[i-1] == Y[j-1]`, that character can extend the best suffix ending at `j - 1` using `X[0..i-1)`: `dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1`. Otherwise `dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j]`.","The answer is the maximum value in the table. Only the previous row is needed; iterate `j` downwards to update a single row in place."],"starters":{"python":"import sys\n\n\ndef longest_len(x: str, y: str) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here\n    return 0\n\n\ndef main():\n    x, y = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    print(longest_len(x, y))\n\n\nmain()\n","javascript":"function longestLen(x, y) {\n  // Write your solution here\n  return 0\n}\n\nconst [x, y] = input.split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean)\nconsole.log(longestLen(x, y))\n","cpp":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint longestLen(const string& x, const string& y) {\n    // Write your solution here\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    string x, y;\n    cin >> x >> y;\n    cout << longestLen(x, y) << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static int longestLen(String x, String y) {\n        // Write your solution here\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String x = br.readLine().trim();\n        String y = br.readLine().trim();\n        System.out.println(longestLen(x, y));\n    }\n}\n"},"reconstructed":false}